# =============================================================================
# BUILD 08 (WORKING): Stateful Auth Session & Rate-Limit Server Engine
# =============================================================================
# Compiled to a native binary (`session_server`) that acts as a persistent
# command-stream daemon with Write-Ahead Log (WAL) crash recovery.
# =============================================================================

Sessions is a collection.
Each session has a token (text), a username (text), a role_level (number), a req_count (number), a quota_limit (number), a expires_at (number) and a revoked (number).
No two sessions share the same token.
If a session already exists, replace it.

An active session is a session whose revoked is 0.
An over_quota session is an active session whose req_count is at least quota_limit.

create-session: add a session.
lookup-session: find a session by token.
destroy-session: remove a session by token.

# Rate-limiting & session lifecycle capabilities
record-hit: for every active session whose token is a given token, increase req_count by 1.
enforce-quotas: for every over_quota session, set revoked to 1.
expire-sessions: for every active session whose expires_at is under a given now_epoch, set revoked to 1.
purge-revoked: keep sessions whose revoked is 0.

active-session-count: how many active sessions are there?
revoked-session-count: how many sessions whose revoked is 1 are there?
top-consumers: show the top 5 active sessions by req_count.
